   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the general municipal law, in relation to bureaus of administrative adjudication",
    "basePrintNo": "S5772",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S5772-2017",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §380, Gen Muni L",
    "lawSection": "General Municipal Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S5772      Revised 6/7/17\n\n TITLE OF BILL :  An act to amend the general municipal law, in\nrelation to bureaus of administrative adjudication\n\n PURPOSE OF BILL :\n\nThis bill will authorize the City of Auburn to create an\nAdministrative Adjudication Bureau to adjudicate code violations.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\n\nSection 1: Adds a new subsection 3 to § 380 of the General Municipal\nLaw authorizing the City of Auburn to adopt a local law to create an\nAdministrative Adjudication Bureau to adjudicate code and ordinance\nviolations that constitute a threat or danger to public health, safety\nor welfare.\n\nSection 2: Establishes the effective date.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nThe Auburn City Housing Court calendar has become overburdened with\ncases prosecuting code violations, including many minor violations.\nThe City seeks to implement the model used in Buffalo and Yonkers to\nadjudicate minor violations though an Administrative Adjudication\nBureau. The Bureau would use Administrative Law Judges to adjudicate\ncode violations in an efficient and expeditious manner. The goal is to\nfree up the resources of the City and the City Housing Court for the\nprosecution of the most serious code and ordinance violations.\nAuburn, like other Upstate cities, is facing an epidemic of absentee\nlandowners that allow their properties to deteriorate and code\nviolations to mount. This bill will give the City a new tool in their\nfight against urban blight.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\nNew bill.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n\nBy improving enforcement of City codes and ordinance violations\nrevenues should increase.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
